### Straight at the Mountebank simulator, bypassing the gateway.
### (AI Generayed) Needs `docker compose up -d`. Note snake_case here vs camelCase on our API.

### Authorized (card ends 7) -> 200, authorized true + a real authorization_code
POST {{bank}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "card_number": "2222405343248877",
  "expiry_date": "04/2030",
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Unauthorized (card ends 4) -> 200, authorized false.
### authorization_code comes back as "" - present but empty, never trust it.
POST {{bank}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "card_number": "2222405343248874",
  "expiry_date": "04/2030",
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Service unavailable (card ends 0) -> 503
POST {{bank}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "card_number": "2222405343248870",
  "expiry_date": "04/2030",
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Missing field -> 400 with an "error_message" key (snake_case)
POST {{bank}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "card_number": "2222405343248877",
  "currency": "GBP",
  "amount": 100,
  "cvv": "123"
}

### Wrong path -> 400 with an "errorMessage" key (camelCase).
### Same status, different body shape - which is why the client only ever
### branches on the status code and never parses the bank's error body.
POST {{bank}}/nope
Content-Type: application/json

{}
